From 97f7dba118555d229d720ce98bbc2fe2ba660127 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Miroslav=20Mr=C3=A1z?= <miroslav.mraz@techmania.cz>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 00:32:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH v1 3/6] media: qcom: camss: Add support for SC7180

Add the CAMSS resources for the Qualcomm SC7180 / SM7125 SoC: four CSIPHYs
(3ph v1.0), three CSIDs (CSID0/1 plus a CSID-lite) and three VFEs (VFE-170,
VFE0/1 plus a VFE-lite), together with the CAMNOC interconnect paths.

A new CAMSS_7180 version is added and handled alongside the other VFE-170
based SoCs in camss-vfe.c.

Based on prior, unmerged work by George Chan for the SM7125 (Redmi 9 Pro).
Link: https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/13709406/

---
